IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sgn-register`

-- Tests for sgn-register.l4 (ss 386AF, 386AFA). Expected values are written from the text beside each assertion.
-- The appointed day is an input (the Act that fixes it is not a source). The tests use 16 June 2025, the date the consolidation's amendment
-- marks show for the 2024 amendments ("Act 23 of 2024 wef 16/06/2025"); that is an assumed test value, not text (finding 4 in NOTES.md).

`s 386AF test the appointed day` MEANS Date 16 6 2025
`s 386AF test company` MEANS Company "Acme Pte Ltd"
`s 386AF test foreign company` MEANS `Foreign company` "Acme Holdings Inc"

§ `s 386AF(8) timing helper`

-- arguments: done; the day it was done; the day the time began; the days allowed; the date asked
-- done on the last day (1 Jan + 30 days = 31 Jan): in time. "not later than 30 days after" includes the last day.
#ASSERT `s 386AF(8) timing: the act was done in time` TRUE (Date 31 1 2020) (Date 1 1 2020) 30 (Date 31 1 2020) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- done a day late
#ASSERT `s 386AF(8) timing: the act was done in time` TRUE (Date 1 2 2020) (Date 1 1 2020) 30 (Date 1 2 2020) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- done on the day of the event itself: in time
#ASSERT `s 386AF(8) timing: the act was done in time` TRUE (Date 1 1 2020) (Date 1 1 2020) 30 (Date 1 2 2020) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not done, and the last day has passed
#ASSERT `s 386AF(8) timing: the act was done in time` FALSE (Date 1 1 2020) (Date 1 1 2020) 30 (Date 1 2 2020) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not done, and the date asked is the last day: not yet late
#ASSERT `s 386AF(8) timing: the act was done in time` FALSE (Date 1 1 2020) (Date 1 1 2020) 30 (Date 31 1 2020) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 386AF(1): incorporated on or after 31 March 2017 but before the appointed day`

-- arguments: the date of incorporation; the appointed day
#ASSERT `s 386AF(1) the last day by which the company must have kept its register` (Date 1 4 2017) `s 386AF test the appointed day` EQUALS JUST (Date 1 5 2017)
-- the first day the subsection covers (31 March 2017) and the last (the day before the appointed day)
#ASSERT `s 386AF(1) the last day by which the company must have kept its register` (Date 31 3 2017) `s 386AF test the appointed day` EQUALS JUST (Date 30 4 2017)
#ASSERT `s 386AF(1) the last day by which the company must have kept its register` (Date 15 6 2025) `s 386AF test the appointed day` EQUALS JUST (Date 15 7 2025)
-- outside: the day before 31 March 2017 is for (2); the appointed day itself is for (1A)
#ASSERT `s 386AF(1) the last day by which the company must have kept its register` (Date 30 3 2017) `s 386AF test the appointed day` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 386AF(1) the last day by which the company must have kept its register` (Date 16 6 2025) `s 386AF test the appointed day` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 386AF(1A): incorporated on or after the appointed day`

#ASSERT `s 386AF(1A) the day on which the company must start to keep its register` (Date 16 6 2025) `s 386AF test the appointed day` EQUALS JUST (Date 16 6 2025)
#ASSERT `s 386AF(1A) the day on which the company must start to keep its register` (Date 1 3 2026) `s 386AF test the appointed day` EQUALS JUST (Date 1 3 2026)
#ASSERT `s 386AF(1A) the day on which the company must start to keep its register` (Date 15 6 2025) `s 386AF test the appointed day` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 386AF(2): incorporated before 31 March 2017`

-- 31 March 2017 plus 60 days: April has 30 days, so the 60th day is 30 May 2017
#ASSERT `s 386AF(2) the last day by which the company must have kept its register` (Date 30 3 2017) EQUALS JUST (Date 30 5 2017)
#ASSERT `s 386AF(2) the last day by which the company must have kept its register` (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS JUST (Date 30 5 2017)
#ASSERT `s 386AF(2) the last day by which the company must have kept its register` (Date 31 3 2017) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 386AF(3): a company that becomes subject to the Part`

-- 10 January 2026 plus 60 days: 21 days to 31 January, 28 to 28 February, 11 more: 11 March 2026
#ASSERT `s 386AF(3) the last day by which the company must have kept its register` TRUE (Date 10 1 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 11 3 2026)
#ASSERT `s 386AF(3) the last day by which the company must have kept its register` FALSE (Date 10 1 2026) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 386AF(1), (1A), (2) and (3) together`

-- arguments: became subject later; the date the Part applies; the date of incorporation; the appointed day
#ASSERT `s 386AF(1), (1A), (2) and (3) the day by which the company must have kept its register` FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 4 2017) `s 386AF test the appointed day` EQUALS JUST (Date 1 5 2017)
#ASSERT `s 386AF(1), (1A), (2) and (3) the day by which the company must have kept its register` FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 3 2017) `s 386AF test the appointed day` EQUALS JUST (Date 30 5 2017)
#ASSERT `s 386AF(1), (1A), (2) and (3) the day by which the company must have kept its register` FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 7 2025) `s 386AF test the appointed day` EQUALS JUST (Date 1 7 2025)
-- where the company became subject later, (3) governs even though (1) or (2) would also fit its date of incorporation (fork F-AF1)
#ASSERT `s 386AF(1), (1A), (2) and (3) the day by which the company must have kept its register` TRUE (Date 10 1 2026) (Date 1 4 2017) `s 386AF test the appointed day` EQUALS JUST (Date 11 3 2026)

-- in time? arguments: as above, then: the register has been kept; the day it was kept; the date asked
#ASSERT `s 386AF(1), (1A), (2) and (3) the company has kept its register in time` FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 4 2017) `s 386AF test the appointed day` TRUE (Date 1 5 2017) (Date 1 6 2017) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 386AF(1), (1A), (2) and (3) the company has kept its register in time` FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 4 2017) `s 386AF test the appointed day` TRUE (Date 2 5 2017) (Date 3 5 2017) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 386AF(1), (1A), (2) and (3) the company has kept its register in time` FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 4 2017) `s 386AF test the appointed day` FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 2 5 2017) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 386AF(1), (1A), (2) and (3) the company has kept its register in time` FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 4 2017) `s 386AF test the appointed day` FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 1 5 2017) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (1A): the register must be kept from the date of incorporation itself
#ASSERT `s 386AF(1), (1A), (2) and (3) the company has kept its register in time` FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 7 2025) `s 386AF test the appointed day` TRUE (Date 1 7 2025) (Date 1 7 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 386AF(1), (1A), (2) and (3) the company has kept its register in time` FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 7 2025) `s 386AF test the appointed day` TRUE (Date 2 7 2025) (Date 2 7 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 386AF(4), (4A), (5), (6): the same for a foreign company`

-- arguments of (4): the date of registration; the appointed day
#ASSERT `s 386AF(4) the last day by which the foreign company must have kept its register` (Date 1 4 2017) `s 386AF test the appointed day` EQUALS JUST (Date 1 5 2017)
#ASSERT `s 386AF(4) the last day by which the foreign company must have kept its register` (Date 30 3 2017) `s 386AF test the appointed day` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 386AF(4) the last day by which the foreign company must have kept its register` (Date 16 6 2025) `s 386AF test the appointed day` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 386AF(4A) the day on which the foreign company must start to keep its register` (Date 16 6 2025) `s 386AF test the appointed day` EQUALS JUST (Date 16 6 2025)
#ASSERT `s 386AF(4A) the day on which the foreign company must start to keep its register` (Date 15 6 2025) `s 386AF test the appointed day` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 386AF(5) the last day by which the foreign company must have kept its register` (Date 30 3 2017) EQUALS JUST (Date 30 5 2017)
#ASSERT `s 386AF(5) the last day by which the foreign company must have kept its register` (Date 31 3 2017) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 386AF(6) the last day by which the foreign company must have kept its register` TRUE (Date 10 1 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 11 3 2026)
#ASSERT `s 386AF(6) the last day by which the foreign company must have kept its register` FALSE (Date 10 1 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- together: became subject later; the date the Part applies; the date of registration; the appointed day
#ASSERT `s 386AF(4), (4A), (5) and (6) the day by which the foreign company must have kept its register` FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 4 2017) `s 386AF test the appointed day` EQUALS JUST (Date 1 5 2017)
#ASSERT `s 386AF(4), (4A), (5) and (6) the day by which the foreign company must have kept its register` FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 3 2017) `s 386AF test the appointed day` EQUALS JUST (Date 30 5 2017)
#ASSERT `s 386AF(4), (4A), (5) and (6) the day by which the foreign company must have kept its register` FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 7 2025) `s 386AF test the appointed day` EQUALS JUST (Date 1 7 2025)
#ASSERT `s 386AF(4), (4A), (5) and (6) the day by which the foreign company must have kept its register` TRUE (Date 10 1 2026) (Date 1 4 2017) `s 386AF test the appointed day` EQUALS JUST (Date 11 3 2026)
-- in time? arguments: as above, then kept; the day kept; the date asked
#ASSERT `s 386AF(4), (4A), (5) and (6) the foreign company has kept its register in time` FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 4 2017) `s 386AF test the appointed day` TRUE (Date 1 5 2017) (Date 1 6 2017) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 386AF(4), (4A), (5) and (6) the foreign company has kept its register in time` FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 4 2017) `s 386AF test the appointed day` TRUE (Date 2 5 2017) (Date 3 5 2017) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 386AF(4), (4A), (5) and (6) the foreign company has kept its register in time` FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 4 2017) `s 386AF test the appointed day` FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 1 5 2017) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 386AF(1) to (6): the duty to keep the register, as regulative rules (the trace clock counts days from the day the time begins)`

-- (1): not later than 30 days after incorporation: day 30 is in time, day 31 is late
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 386AF(1) a company incorporated on or after 31 March 2017 but before the appointed day must keep a register not later than 30 days after incorporation` `s 386AF test company` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 386AF test company` DOES `s 386AF(1) to (6) keep a register of its registrable controllers` AT 30
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 386AF(1) a company incorporated on or after 31 March 2017 but before the appointed day must keep a register not later than 30 days after incorporation` `s 386AF test company` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 386AF test company` DOES `s 386AF(1) to (6) keep a register of its registrable controllers` AT 31
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 386AF(1) a company incorporated on or after 31 March 2017 but before the appointed day must keep a register not later than 30 days after incorporation` `s 386AF test company` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 31)
-- (1A): starting on the date of incorporation: day 0 only
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 386AF(1A) a company incorporated on or after the appointed day must keep a register starting on the date of incorporation` `s 386AF test company` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 386AF test company` DOES `s 386AF(1) to (6) keep a register of its registrable controllers` AT 0
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 386AF(1A) a company incorporated on or after the appointed day must keep a register starting on the date of incorporation` `s 386AF test company` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 386AF test company` DOES `s 386AF(1) to (6) keep a register of its registrable controllers` AT 1
-- (2): 60 days after 31 March 2017
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 386AF(2) a company incorporated before 31 March 2017 must keep a register not later than 60 days after that date` `s 386AF test company` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 386AF test company` DOES `s 386AF(1) to (6) keep a register of its registrable controllers` AT 60
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 386AF(2) a company incorporated before 31 March 2017 must keep a register not later than 60 days after that date` `s 386AF test company` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 386AF test company` DOES `s 386AF(1) to (6) keep a register of its registrable controllers` AT 61
-- (3)
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 386AF(3) a company that becomes subject to this Part must keep a register not later than 60 days after the Part applies or re-applies` `s 386AF test company` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 386AF test company` DOES `s 386AF(1) to (6) keep a register of its registrable controllers` AT 60
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 386AF(3) a company that becomes subject to this Part must keep a register not later than 60 days after the Part applies or re-applies` `s 386AF test company` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 386AF test company` DOES `s 386AF(1) to (6) keep a register of its registrable controllers` AT 61
-- (4), (4A), (5), (6): the same for a foreign company
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 386AF(4) a foreign company registered on or after 31 March 2017 but before the appointed day must keep a register not later than 30 days after registration` `s 386AF test foreign company` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 386AF test foreign company` DOES `s 386AF(1) to (6) keep a register of its registrable controllers` AT 30
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 386AF(4) a foreign company registered on or after 31 March 2017 but before the appointed day must keep a register not later than 30 days after registration` `s 386AF test foreign company` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 386AF test foreign company` DOES `s 386AF(1) to (6) keep a register of its registrable controllers` AT 31
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 386AF(4A) a foreign company registered on or after the appointed day must keep a register starting on the date of registration` `s 386AF test foreign company` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 386AF test foreign company` DOES `s 386AF(1) to (6) keep a register of its registrable controllers` AT 0
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 386AF(4A) a foreign company registered on or after the appointed day must keep a register starting on the date of registration` `s 386AF test foreign company` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 386AF test foreign company` DOES `s 386AF(1) to (6) keep a register of its registrable controllers` AT 1
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 386AF(5) a foreign company registered before 31 March 2017 must keep a register not later than 60 days after that date` `s 386AF test foreign company` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 386AF test foreign company` DOES `s 386AF(1) to (6) keep a register of its registrable controllers` AT 60
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 386AF(5) a foreign company registered before 31 March 2017 must keep a register not later than 60 days after that date` `s 386AF test foreign company` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 386AF test foreign company` DOES `s 386AF(1) to (6) keep a register of its registrable controllers` AT 61
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 386AF(6) a foreign company that becomes subject to this Part must keep a register not later than 60 days after the Part applies or re-applies` `s 386AF test foreign company` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 386AF test foreign company` DOES `s 386AF(1) to (6) keep a register of its registrable controllers` AT 60
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 386AF(6) a foreign company that becomes subject to this Part must keep a register not later than 60 days after the Part applies or re-applies` `s 386AF test foreign company` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 386AF test foreign company` DOES `s 386AF(1) to (6) keep a register of its registrable controllers` AT 61

§ `s 386AF(7): what the register must hold`

-- arguments: has the prescribed particulars; (3) of s 386AFA applies; has the note; a change has occurred; updated for it; form and place
#ASSERT `s 386AF(7) the register is as the subsection requires` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (aa) applies and the register has the note
#ASSERT `s 386AF(7) the register is as the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (aa) applies and the register lacks the note
#ASSERT `s 386AF(7) the register is as the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (b) a change occurred and the register was updated; and not updated
#ASSERT `s 386AF(7) the register is as the subsection requires` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 386AF(7) the register is as the subsection requires` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (a) the particulars are missing
#ASSERT `s 386AF(7) the register is as the subsection requires` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (c) the wrong form or place
#ASSERT `s 386AF(7) the register is as the subsection requires` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- (7) as duties without a time limit: nothing in the subsection can make them breached by lateness. The trace shows the duty, fulfilled when done.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 386AF(7)(a) a company or foreign company must ensure that its register contains the prescribed particulars` `s 386AF test company` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 386AF test company` DOES `s 386AF(7)(a) ensure that the register contains the prescribed particulars of its registrable individual controllers and registrable corporate controllers` AT 3
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 386AF(7)(a) a company or foreign company must ensure that its register contains the prescribed particulars` `s 386AF test company` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 400)
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 386AF(7)(aa) a company or foreign company must ensure that its register contains the note and particulars required under section 386AFA(3)` `s 386AF test company` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 386AF test company` DOES `s 386AF(7)(aa) ensure that the register contains the note and prescribed particulars required under section 386AFA(3), if applicable` AT 3
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 386AF(7)(b) a company or foreign company must ensure that its register is updated if any change occurs` `s 386AF test company` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 386AF test company` DOES `s 386AF(7)(b) ensure that the register is updated if any change to the prescribed particulars occurs` AT 3
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 386AF(7)(c) a company or foreign company must ensure that its register is kept in the prescribed form and at the prescribed place` `s 386AF test company` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 386AF test company` DOES `s 386AF(7)(c) ensure that the register is kept in the prescribed form and at the prescribed place` AT 3

§ `s 386AF(8): enter the particulars and update the register within the prescribed time and in the prescribed manner`

-- arguments: done; the day done; the day the prescribed time runs from; the prescribed time in days; in the prescribed manner; the date asked
-- done in time and in the prescribed manner (14 days from 1 June 2026: the last day is 15 June 2026)
#ASSERT `s 386AF(8) the company or foreign company has entered the particulars and updated the register in time and in the prescribed manner` TRUE (Date 15 6 2026) (Date 1 6 2026) 14 TRUE (Date 20 6 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- done a day late
#ASSERT `s 386AF(8) the company or foreign company has entered the particulars and updated the register in time and in the prescribed manner` TRUE (Date 16 6 2026) (Date 1 6 2026) 14 TRUE (Date 20 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- done in time but not in the prescribed manner
#ASSERT `s 386AF(8) the company or foreign company has entered the particulars and updated the register in time and in the prescribed manner` TRUE (Date 10 6 2026) (Date 1 6 2026) 14 FALSE (Date 20 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not done: last day passed / not yet passed
#ASSERT `s 386AF(8) the company or foreign company has entered the particulars and updated the register in time and in the prescribed manner` FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 1 6 2026) 14 FALSE (Date 16 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 386AF(8) the company or foreign company has entered the particulars and updated the register in time and in the prescribed manner` FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 1 6 2026) 14 FALSE (Date 15 6 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- the rule, with a prescribed time of 14 days
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 386AF(8) a company or foreign company must enter the particulars and update its register within the prescribed time` `s 386AF test company` 14 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 386AF test company` DOES `s 386AF(8) enter the particulars in the register and update the register` AT 14
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 386AF(8) a company or foreign company must enter the particulars and update its register within the prescribed time` `s 386AF test company` 14 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 386AF test company` DOES `s 386AF(8) enter the particulars in the register and update the register` AT 15

§ `s 386AF(9) and (10): entering a controller's particulars`

-- arguments: the controller has confirmed; the company entered or updated; the entry carries the "not confirmed" note
#ASSERT `s 386AF(9) the company or foreign company has done what the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no confirmation, entered with the note: paragraph (b)
#ASSERT `s 386AF(9) the company or foreign company has done what the subsection requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no confirmation, entered without the note
#ASSERT `s 386AF(9) the company or foreign company has done what the subsection requires` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- nothing entered yet: the subsection fixes no time
#ASSERT `s 386AF(9) the company or foreign company has done what the subsection requires` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 386AF(9) the company or foreign company has done what the subsection requires` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 386AF(10) the controller's confirmation is a confirmation for the purposes of subsection (9)(a)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 386AF(10) the controller's confirmation is a confirmation for the purposes of subsection (9)(a)` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 386AF(9)(a) a company or foreign company must enter or update the particulars of a controller after the controller confirms them` `s 386AF test company` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 386AF test company` DOES `s 386AF(9)(a) enter or update the particulars of a controller after the controller has confirmed them` AT 5
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 386AF(9)(b) a company or foreign company that does not receive the confirmation must enter or update the particulars with a note` `s 386AF test company` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 386AF test company` DOES `s 386AF(9)(b) enter or update the particulars of a controller with a note that they have not been confirmed by the controller` AT 5

§ `s 386AF(11): the register is not to be shown to a member of the public`

-- arguments: the person is a member of the public; the disclosure is a requirement or exercise of a power under s 386AM
#ASSERT `s 386AF(11) the company or foreign company is barred from disclosing the register to the person` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a member of the company acting as such is a member of the public (s 386AB), so the bar reaches the member
#ASSERT `s 386AF(11) the company or foreign company is barred from disclosing the register to the person` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a requirement under s 386AM lifts the bar
#ASSERT `s 386AF(11) the company or foreign company is barred from disclosing the register to the person` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 386AF(11) the company or foreign company is barred from disclosing the register to the person` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not a member of the public: the bar does not speak of the person
#ASSERT `s 386AF(11) the company or foreign company is barred from disclosing the register to the person` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the prohibition: disclosing is the breach
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 386AF(11) a company or foreign company must not disclose the register to a member of the public` `s 386AF test company` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 386AF test company` DOES `s 386AF(11) disclose the register or any particulars in it, or make it available for inspection, to a member of the public` AT 9
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 386AF(11) a company or foreign company must not disclose the register to a member of the public` `s 386AF test company` AT 0 WITH

§ `s 386AF(12) and (13): the offences`

-- arguments: fails (1), (1A), (2) or (3); fails (7), (8), (9) or (11)
#ASSERT `s 386AF(12) the company is guilty of the offence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 386AF(12) the company is guilty of the offence` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 386AF(12) the company is guilty of the offence` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the officer: arguments: the two failures; the person is an officer in default (s 408(3))
#ASSERT `s 386AF(12) the officer of the company is guilty of the offence` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 386AF(12) the officer of the company is guilty of the offence` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 386AF(12) the officer of the company is guilty of the offence` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 386AF(12) the officer of the company is guilty of the offence` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the penalty: a fine not exceeding $25,000, no imprisonment, no default penalty stated. arguments: the two failures; the person is the company; the person is an officer in default
#ASSERT `s 386AF(12) the most the company or an officer in default may be sentenced to on conviction` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST (Penalty OF 25000, 0, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 386AF(12) the most the company or an officer in default may be sentenced to on conviction` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST (Penalty OF 25000, 0, FALSE, FALSE)
-- no failure: no penalty is stated
#ASSERT `s 386AF(12) the most the company or an officer in default may be sentenced to on conviction` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- an officer not in default: no penalty is stated
#ASSERT `s 386AF(12) the most the company or an officer in default may be sentenced to on conviction` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 386AF(13), a foreign company
#ASSERT `s 386AF(13) the foreign company is guilty of the offence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 386AF(13) the foreign company is guilty of the offence` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 386AF(13) the foreign company is guilty of the offence` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 386AF(13) the officer of the foreign company is guilty of the offence` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 386AF(13) the officer of the foreign company is guilty of the offence` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 386AF(13) the officer of the foreign company is guilty of the offence` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 386AF(13) the most the foreign company or an officer in default may be sentenced to on conviction` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST (Penalty OF 25000, 0, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 386AF(13) the most the foreign company or an officer in default may be sentenced to on conviction` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST (Penalty OF 25000, 0, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 386AF(13) the most the foreign company or an officer in default may be sentenced to on conviction` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 386AF(14): the appointed day is the date of commencement of section 4 of the 2024 Act, supplied
#ASSERT `s 386AF(14) "appointed day" the appointed day` (Date 16 6 2025) EQUALS (Date 16 6 2025)

§ `s 386AFA(1): when the section applies`

-- arguments: knows (or has reasonable grounds to believe) it has no registrable controller; knows it has one but cannot identify it
#ASSERT `s 386AFA(1) this section applies to the company or foreign company` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 386AFA(1) this section applies to the company or foreign company` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 386AFA(1) this section applies to the company or foreign company` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 386AFA(8): the definitions`

#ASSERT `s 386AFA(8) "chief executive officer" the person is a chief executive officer of the company or foreign company` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 386AFA(8) "chief executive officer" the person is a chief executive officer of the company or foreign company` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 386AFA(8) "chief executive officer" the person is a chief executive officer of the company or foreign company` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 386AFA(8) "director with executive control" the person is a director with executive control` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 386AFA(8) "director with executive control" the person is a director with executive control` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 386AFA(8) "director with executive control" the person is a director with executive control` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 386AFA(2): who is taken to be a registrable controller`

-- arguments: the section applies; the person is a director with executive control; the person is a chief executive officer
#ASSERT `s 386AFA(2) the person is taken to be a registrable controller of the company or foreign company for the purposes of this Part` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 386AFA(2) the person is taken to be a registrable controller of the company or foreign company for the purposes of this Part` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the section applies but the person is neither
#ASSERT `s 386AFA(2) the person is taken to be a registrable controller of the company or foreign company for the purposes of this Part` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the section does not apply
#ASSERT `s 386AFA(2) the person is taken to be a registrable controller of the company or foreign company for the purposes of this Part` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 386AFA(3): the note and the particulars`

-- arguments: the section applies; the note entered; the prescribed particulars entered
#ASSERT `s 386AFA(3) the company or foreign company has entered in its register what the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 386AFA(3) the company or foreign company has entered in its register what the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 386AFA(3) the company or foreign company has entered in its register what the subsection requires` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 386AFA(3) the company or foreign company has entered in its register what the subsection requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 386AFA(3) a company or foreign company to which the section applies must enter the note and the prescribed particulars` `s 386AF test company` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 386AF test company` DOES `s 386AFA(3) enter in the register of controllers the note and the prescribed particulars of each director with executive control and each chief executive officer` AT 3
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 386AFA(3) a company or foreign company to which the section applies must enter the note and the prescribed particulars` `s 386AF test company` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 400)

§ `s 386AFA(4): enter the matters within the prescribed period`

-- arguments: the case; the date the company knows it has no registrable controller; the date it forms the opinion it cannot identify one; entered; the day entered; the prescribed period in days; the date asked
-- (a): knows on 1 March 2026; prescribed period 14 days: the last day is 15 March 2026
#ASSERT `s 386AFA(4) the company or foreign company has entered the matters within the prescribed period` `s 386AFA(4)(a) the company or foreign company knows, or has reasonable grounds to believe, that it has no registrable controller` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) TRUE (Date 15 3 2026) 14 (Date 20 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 386AFA(4) the company or foreign company has entered the matters within the prescribed period` `s 386AFA(4)(a) the company or foreign company knows, or has reasonable grounds to believe, that it has no registrable controller` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) TRUE (Date 16 3 2026) 14 (Date 20 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (b): the period runs from the date of the opinion (1 April 2026), not from the date in (a)
#ASSERT `s 386AFA(4) the company or foreign company has entered the matters within the prescribed period` `s 386AFA(4)(b) the company or foreign company has a registrable controller it has not been able to identify` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 4 2026) TRUE (Date 15 4 2026) 14 (Date 20 4 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 386AFA(4) the company or foreign company has entered the matters within the prescribed period` `s 386AFA(4)(b) the company or foreign company has a registrable controller it has not been able to identify` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 4 2026) TRUE (Date 16 4 2026) 14 (Date 20 4 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not entered: the period has run out, or has not
#ASSERT `s 386AFA(4) the company or foreign company has entered the matters within the prescribed period` `s 386AFA(4)(a) the company or foreign company knows, or has reasonable grounds to believe, that it has no registrable controller` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) 14 (Date 16 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 386AFA(4) the company or foreign company has entered the matters within the prescribed period` `s 386AFA(4)(a) the company or foreign company knows, or has reasonable grounds to believe, that it has no registrable controller` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) 14 (Date 15 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 386AFA(4) a company or foreign company must enter the matters mentioned in subsection (3) within the prescribed period` `s 386AF test company` 14 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 386AF test company` DOES `s 386AFA(3) enter in the register of controllers the note and the prescribed particulars of each director with executive control and each chief executive officer` AT 14
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 386AFA(4) a company or foreign company must enter the matters mentioned in subsection (3) within the prescribed period` `s 386AF test company` 14 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 386AF test company` DOES `s 386AFA(3) enter in the register of controllers the note and the prescribed particulars of each director with executive control and each chief executive officer` AT 15

§ `s 386AFA(5): update the register after a change`

-- arguments: the date the company knows of the change; updated; the day updated; the prescribed period in days; the date asked
#ASSERT `s 386AFA(5) the company or foreign company has updated its register within the prescribed period` (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE (Date 15 3 2026) 14 (Date 20 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 386AFA(5) the company or foreign company has updated its register within the prescribed period` (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE (Date 16 3 2026) 14 (Date 20 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 386AFA(5) the company or foreign company has updated its register within the prescribed period` (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) 14 (Date 16 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 386AFA(5) the company or foreign company has updated its register within the prescribed period` (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) 14 (Date 15 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 386AFA(5) a company or foreign company must update its register of controllers within the prescribed period after it knows of a change` `s 386AF test company` 14 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 386AF test company` DOES `s 386AFA(5) update the register of controllers to reflect a change in the particulars entered under subsection (3)(b)` AT 14
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 386AFA(5) a company or foreign company must update its register of controllers within the prescribed period after it knows of a change` `s 386AF test company` 14 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 386AF test company` DOES `s 386AFA(5) update the register of controllers to reflect a change in the particulars entered under subsection (3)(b)` AT 15

